    },
    {
      "key": "capture",
      "icon": "file",
      "title": "Recorded capture",
      "nodeClass": "card",
      "summary": "Replays a saved session. No hardware, no card, repeatable.",
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "terminal",
          "channel": "apdu",
          "role": "responder",
          "label": "terminal"
        }
      ],
      "device": "file",
      "latencyMs": 0,
      "fields": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "key": "path",
          "label": "Capture file",
          "placeholder": "logs/session-2026-09-11.jsonl",
          "reaches": "file"
        },
        {
          "kind": "bool",
          "key": "strict",
          "label": "Strict replay",
          "default": true,
          "help": "Fail on a command the capture does not contain, rather than improvising a response."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "iso8583.replay",
      "icon": "file",
      "title": "Corpus replay",
      "nodeClass": "host",
      "summary": "Plays the acquirer from a captured conversation, with nothing in front of it.",
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "host",
          "channel": "iso8583",
          "role": "requester",
          "label": "host"
        }
      ],
      "device": "file",
      "latencyMs": 0,
      "fields": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "key": "corpus",
          "label": "Corpus file",
          "placeholder": "captures/auth-2026-09-11.jsonl",
          "reaches": "file"
        },
        {
          "kind": "select",
          "key": "mode",
          "label": "Mode",
          "default": "verbatim",
          "options": [
            {
              "value": "verbatim",
              "label": "Verbatim — resend exactly what was captured"
            },
            {
              "value": "freshen",
              "label": "Freshen — new STAN, RRN and timestamps"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "caveats": [
        "Verbatim resends a STAN and RRN the host has already seen. A host that approves a byte-identical replay has no duplicate detection at all, which is the question it asks.",
        "Freshen rewrites only the volatile routing fields and leaves DE55 and its cryptogram exactly as captured — so it asks whether the ARQC is really bound to them."
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "iso8583.host",
      "icon": "link",
      "title": "Payment host",
      "nodeClass": "host",
      "summary": "An acquirer, gateway or issuer reached over TCP with MLI framing.",
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "acquirer",
          "channel": "iso8583",
          "role": "responder",
          "label": "acquirer"
        }
      ],
      "latencyMs": 40,
      "fields": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "key": "host",
          "label": "Host",
          "placeholder": "switch.test.local"
        },
        {
          "kind": "number",
          "key": "port",
          "label": "Port",
          "default": 8583,
          "min": 1,
          "max": 65535
        },
        {
          "kind": "select",
          "key": "dialect",
          "label": "Dialect",
          "default": "iso8583-1987",
          "options": [
            {
              "value": "iso8583-1987",
              "label": "ISO 8583:1987"
            },
            {
              "value": "base24",
              "label": "BASE24"
            },
            {
              "value": "postilion",
              "label": "Postilion"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "bool",
          "key": "tls",
          "label": "TLS",
          "default": false
        }
      ],
      "caveats": [
        "A dialect is a guess about somebody else's system. Getting the framing wrong degrades to \"could not read that\" rather than to a corrupted link."
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "iso8583.mutation",
      "icon": "swap",
      "title": "Host mutation",
      "nodeClass": "host",
      "summary": "Rewrites data elements and DE55 tags as an authorisation passes.",
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "acquirer",
          "channel": "iso8583",
          "role": "responder",
          "label": "acquirer"
        },
        {
          "id": "host",
          "channel": "iso8583",
          "role": "requester",
          "label": "host"
        }
      ],
      "latencyMs": 1,
      "fields": [
        {
          "kind": "yaml",
          "key": "playbook",
          "label": "Playbook",
          "default": "# Host mutation rules, in atrium's host playbook format.\n# Playbooks from atrium/host/playbooks/ paste in here unchanged.\nname: amount-mismatch\ndescription: Raise DE4 while leaving the cryptogram's own amount untouched.\nenabled: true\n\nfield_mutations:\n  - de: 4\n    mode: replace\n    value: \"000000009999\"\n    direction: acquirer->issuer\n    on_mti: [\"0100\", \"0200\"]\n    comment: \"DE4 -> 99.99; tag 9F02 still carries the signed amount\"\n\nde55_mutations: []\n",
          "rows": 18
        },
        {
          "kind": "bool",
          "key": "logMutations",
          "label": "Log every rewrite",
          "default": true
        }
      ],
      "caveats": [
        "A rewritten message is re-encoded from its decoded form, so the byte-exactness a passive relay guarantees is given up for the messages a rule actually changed. One that did not decode cleanly is never mutated, and a failed re-encode forwards the original."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
